.TH MD_SET_FREQUENCY 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_set_frequency \- pin a nonzero frequency or release the current pin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_set_frequency(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, double hz);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pin a nonzero frequency or release the current pin.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I hz
Nonzero requested frequency in Hz; signed IF offset for I/Q. Exactly zero
requests unpinning.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder, non-finite hz, negative nonzero audio frequency, or a flushed
handle.
.TP
.B ENOSPC
A new tracking slot is needed but all slots are occupied.
.SH REMARKS
For nonzero hz, behaves as md_pin_frequency(). Negative values are accepted
only on I/Q handles. For zero, behaves as md_unpin_frequency(), including when
zero is negative floating-point zero. To select a carrier exactly at the IF
center, use md_pin_frequency(decoder, 0); this function reserves zero as the
release operation. Pinning selects a channel rather than translating the input
frequency.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_pin_frequency (3),
.BR md_unpin_frequency (3),
.BR md_get_frequency (3)
